    <div class="gfg12-doc">
        <div class="gfg12-sidebar"><span class="gfg12-pagenum">11</span></div>

        <div class="gfg12-main">

            <!-- ==========================================
                 SECTION A: TSP - Thrift Savings Plan
                 ========================================== -->
            <h1 class="gfg12-title">TSP - Thrift Savings Plan</h1>
            <div class="gfg12-accent"></div>

            <p class="gfg12-body">
                The Thrift Savings Plan (TSP) is a retirement savings and investment plan for Federal employees and
                members of the uniformed services, including the Ready Reserve. It was established by Congress in the
                Federal Employees&apos; Retirement System Act of 1986. For FERS employees, TSP is one of a
                three-part retirement package that also includes your FERS basic annuity and Social Security. For a
                FERS employee to take full advantage of this plan, they should contribute 5% to receive the full
                matching benefit. CSRS employees receive no matching funds.
            </p>

            <!-- Three-column block -->
            <div class="gfg12-three-col">

                <!-- Column 1: Contribution Limits (labels) + Current (values) -->
                <div class="gfg12-col-left">
                    <div class="gfg12-contrib-headers">
                        <span class="gfg12-col-heading">Contribution Limits</span>
                        <span class="gfg12-col-heading gfg12-col-heading--center">Current</span>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="gfg12-bullets">
                        <li>
                            <div class="gfg12-contrib-label">
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-name">Regular Contribution</span>
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-val">
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}">
                                        <apex:param value="{!currentYear.Regular_Contribution__c}" />
                                    </apex:outputText>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="gfg12-contrib-label">
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-name">Catch-Up Contribution</span>
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-val">
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}">
                                        <apex:param value="{!currentYear.Catch_Up_Contribution__c}" />
                                    </apex:outputText>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                            <p class="gfg12-sublabel">for employees over age 50</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="gfg12-contrib-label">
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-name">Total Contribution</span>
                                <span class="gfg12-contrib-val">
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}">
                                        <apex:param value="{!totalContribution}" />
                                    </apex:outputText>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="gfg12-contrib-note">
                        Visit <a href="https://www.tsp.gov/making-contributions/contribution-limits/" class="gfg12-link">https://www.tsp.gov/making-contributions/contribution-limits/</a>
                        or scan the QR code for <u>current</u> Contribution Limits
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Column 2: QR Code (no header) -->
                <div class="gfg12-col-middle">
                    <div class="gfg12-qr-wrap">
                        <apex:image url="{!$Resource.Pg12GrovesQR}" width="110" height="110"
                            alt="Current Contribution Limits QR" />
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Column 3: Government Matching Contributions -->
                <div class="gfg12-col-right">
                    <p class="gfg12-col-heading">Government Matching Contributions</p>
                    <ul class="gfg12-bullets">
                        <li>CSRS and CSRS Offset employees receive no matching funds</li>
                        <li>
                            FERS employees receive up to 5% of personal contributions
                            <ul class="gfg12-bullets--circle">
                                <li>1% agency automatic contribution</li>
                                <li>1%-3% of employee contributions are matched at 100%</li>
                                <li>4%-5% of employee contributions are matched at 50%</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

            </div><!-- /gfg12-three-col -->

            <!-- TSP Options in Retirement -->
            <div class="gfg12-options-block">
                <p class="gfg12-options-heading">TSP Options in Retirement</p>
                <div class="gfg12-options-grid">
                    <span class="gfg12-option-item">Monthly Payments</span>
                    <span class="gfg12-option-item">Rollover</span>
                    <span class="gfg12-option-item">Annuitize</span>
                    <span class="gfg12-option-item">Do Nothing</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==========================================
                 SECTION B: Resources
                 ========================================== -->
            <div class="gfg12-section-spacer">
                <h1 class="gfg12-title gfg12-title--sub">Resources</h1>
                <div class="gfg12-accent"></div>

                <p class="gfg12-body">
                    Information in this workbook came from many sources (see below) and, due to time and space, has
                    been condensed to offer you a basic overview. It is not meant to provide a detailed explanation
                    of all benefits. Below are links with extensive information on the benefits which we covered
                    during our review. Should you have additional questions, please review these links and contact us
                    so we may assist you further.
                </p>

                <div class="gfg12-link-item">Federal Retirement: <a href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/publications-forms/pamphlets/ri90-8.pdf" class="gfg12-link">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/publications-forms/pamphlets/ri90-8.pdf</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">FERS: <a href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/fers-information/" class="gfg12-link">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/fers-information/</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">CSRS: <a href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/csrs-information/" class="gfg12-link">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/csrs-information/</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">FEGLI: <a href="http://www.opm.gov/healthcare-insurance/life-insurance/" class="gfg12-link">http://www.opm.gov/healthcare-insurance/life-insurance/</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">TSP: <a href="https://www.tsp.gov/index.html" class="gfg12-link">https://www.tsp.gov/index.html</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">Social Security: <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/" class="gfg12-link">https://www.ssa.gov/</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">Windfall Elimination Provision (WEP): <a href="http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10045.pdf" class="gfg12-link">http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10045.pdf</a></div>
                <div class="gfg12-link-item">Government Pension Offset (GPO): <a href="http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10007.pdf" class="gfg12-link">http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10007.pdf</a></div>
            </div>

